"https://www.meetup.com/casual-moves-and-coffee-house-chess/events/316495819/","description":"**UPDATE: This event has been rescheduled and is now set to begin at 5:00 PM on Sun, Oct 4 (local time).**\n\nVirtual speed dating hosted over Zoom for singles residing in Kitchener. Enjoy rapid individual sessions organized by age group without leaving the comfort of your home.\n\nSimply confirm your attendance and we will contact you with every necessary detail. Availability is restricted and the gathering might be called off if attendance is insufficient.","startDate":"2026-10-04T05:14:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"51 Gamble Ave","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"51 Gamble Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Casual Moves and Coffee House Chess","url":"https://www.meetup.com/casual-moves-and-coffee-house-chess/"},"performer":"Casual Moves and Coffee House Chess"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Morningside salmon run (11 km)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/hike-to-eat/events/316495668/","description":"Salmon will be doing the running, not us. Late September to October is the season for watching salmon swimming upstream. There are four places in Toronto to see the salmon jump but Morningside is the only one that has a festival for it. In fact, this hike happens on that day!\n\nToronto Region Conservation Authority will be conducting guided walks. If interested, sign up at [TRCA](https://trca.ca/salmon-adventures/). We're not affiliated with them and this hike will start after the festival.\n\nFor our hike, we'll start at a clutch of restaurants near Colonel Danforth Park and follow Highland Creek upstream.\n\nIf there's anything more attractive than the salmon migration, it's food. We'll skip the main section of Morningside Park and visit restaurants around Morningside Ave and Lawrence Ave. Then, it's back to nature and ravines. We'll end at Toronto's only Czech restaurant in a lush hideaway, where you can try the different dumplings of Central Europe.\n\n**Highlights**\n\n1. Shamrock Burgers (depart 2:30pm)\n2. Mark's Pizzas\n3. Colonel Danforth Park\n4. Miller Lash House\n5. Morningside Park\n6. The Suya Spot / Amira's Hot Roti and Doubles / Spice Club / Homies Doughnuts (depart 4pm)\n7. St. Margaret in-the-Pines\n8. Lawrence Ave bridge overlooking Highland Creek\n9. Simi African Food Market / Upali Caters (depart 4:45pm)\n10. Highland Creek Park\n11. Cedar Ridge Creative Centre\n12. Prague Restaurant (arrive 5:40pm)\n\n**Neighbourhoods**\nHighland Creek > West Hill > Golfdale Gardens\n\n**Map**\n[https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=1g6tIwKCmtHbLqMdGmwgwWTawibbrD2A&usp=sharing](https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=1g6tIwKCmtHbLqMdGmwgwWTawibbrD2A&usp=sharing)\n\nMultiple moderate climbs: downhill to Colonel Danforth Park, uphill from Morningside Park, down- and uphill from Highland Creek Park.\n\nThe end point is 1 km from the nearest bus stop.\n\n**How it works**\nHike starts punctually. Late or can't do the whole route? Meet us at scheduled checkpoints.\n\nWe'll browse many food places but won't linger long. See the route in advance, organize takeout, then pickup along the way.\n\nNot sure what to try? Join our omakase for $5, which gives a tiny sample from different restaurants. Payment on the day of event by cash or e-transfer to globaltorontoeats@gmail.com. No refunds after orders are placed. Details of sampled food will be uploaded after the hike.\n\nLimited cutlery provided. Highly recommended to bring cutlery and containers for omakase and bringing back leftovers.\n\nSee our [home page](https://www.meetup.com/hike-to-eat/) for more info.","startDate":"2026-10-04T18:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Shamrock Burgers","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Scarborough","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"6109 Kingston Rd, Scarborough, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Hike to Eat","url":"https://www.meetup.com/hike-to-eat/"},"performer":"Hike to Eat"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Downtown Toronto French conversation exchange","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-toronto-french-conversation-exchange/events/316272812/","description":"This is an informal conversation group for anyone wanting to practice / use their French and meet some new people. All levels are welcome, but having a conversational level is strongly recommended (and of course native French speakers are very welcome too!). / Il s'agit d'un groupe de conversation informel pour toute personne souhaitant pratiquer / utiliser son français et rencontrer de nouvelles personnes. Tous les niveaux sont les bienvenus, mais il est recommandé d'avoir un niveau de conversation approximatif (et bien sûr, les locuteurs natifs du français sont également les bienvenus !)\n\nNous nous rencontrerons dimanche, de 14h00 à 16h00, au foodcourt de Brookfield Place, qui heureusement a beaucoup de tables et garde la musique basse!\n\n+ Juste un rappel que ce groupe est un lieu d'échange détendu avec les autres dans un esprit de respect, de tolérance et de réceptivité à la multiplicité des cultures et des niveaux de français représentés. Merci de respecter ces principes en participant aux meetups.","startDate":"2026-10-04T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Brookfield Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"181 Bay St., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Downtown Toronto French conversation exchange","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-toronto-french-conversation-exchange/"},"performer":"Downtown Toronto French conversation exchange"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Richmond Hill Quick Dates for Local Introverts","url":"https://www.meetup.com/clay-buddies-pottery-and-social-club/events/316525158/","description":"**UPDATE: This gathering has been rescheduled and is now set to begin at 5:00 PM on Sun, Oct 4 (local time).**\n\nVirtual speed dating hosted via Zoom for single residents of Richmond Hill. Experience rapid individual rounds tailored by age bracket, all from the comfort of your own home.\n\nSimply submit your RSVP and we will contact you with the complete information. Availability is restricted and the event might be called off if participation is insufficient.","startDate":"2026-10-04T07:58:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"HMF2+V3 Toronto","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"HMF2+V3 Toronto, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Clay Buddies Pottery And Social Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/clay-buddies-pottery-and-social-club/"},"performer":"Clay Buddies Pottery And Social Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Sunday with Friends Autumn Colours Walk Through High Park (meet La Diperie Cafe)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/events/316201381/","description":"Hello everyone,\n\n**\\*\\*Please kindly read carefully- Thank you\\*\\***\n\nPlease join me and my other groups for a fun and leisure autumn colours nature walk through **High Park.**\n\nWe will meet at **La Diperie Cafe** where you are welcome to grab a coffee, water, pastry or ice cream if you like before we head out.\n\nThis will give us an opportunity to introduce ourselves as everyone arrives; then make our way on a friendly walk through the iconic **High Park in Toronto.**\n\nEvent Details below:\n\nSincerely,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n\nEvent Details:\n**Sunday with Friends Autumn Colours Walk Through High Park (Meet at La Diperie Cafe) (Meet at La Diperie Cafe)**\n\n\\*We can stop and rest at different spots, take some photos and share some laughs\n\\*Play a couple ice-breaker games as well to help build some bonds and make connections\n\\*This fun, leisure walk will be a great way to make new friends, appreciate the changing seasons, get some fresh air, and even get a little exercise. :)\n\n**Event Fee:** 10 dollars when you arrive at the La Diperie Cafe (cash only please)\nor e transfer in advance to **steveflemming11@gmail.com**\n\\*If you can't attend walk, but wish to attend mingle after please email me or text me- event fee still applies\n\n\\*I encourage you to take the subway as it is very close to the cafe but certainly driving in an option\n\\*Street parking will be found along Bloor Street and residential area but not inside the park\n\n**Time and Location: Where to meet us?**\n\nMeet us at **La Diperie Cafe** at 3:00 p.m.\n(we will wait for everyone until 3:30 pm)\n**Address:** 1960 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M4W 1J2\nVery close to the High Park Subway station\n(we will then head out for our walk at that point)","startDate":"2026-10-04T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"La Diperie","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"on","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Address: 1960 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON, Toronto, on"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/"},"performer":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Drumming Circle & Uplifting Discussion 🪘✨🌍","url":"https://www.meetup.com/art-soul/events/316164061/","description":"**NO MUSICAL EXPERIENCE REQUIRED**\n\n**About Drum & Soul**\nDrum & Soul is a participatory community space that combines drumming, singing, reflection and conversation in one shared experience. Through rhythms from different cultures, collective music making and meaningful discussion around a focused theme, we practise qualities that strengthen both the individual and the community.\n\nThis is more than a drumming circle. It is a space where people can grow in expression, presence, listening, and contribution, while learning how these same qualities can be carried into everyday life and relationships.\n---\n\n...\n**Why come**\nCome if you want to grow your expressive capacity, feel more at ease participating with others, and be part of a growing space that celebrates the human in us. Everyone is welcome, regardless of age, background or musical experience.\n\nIf you feel shy in groups, that is completely natural. Many people arrive unsure and leave feeling surprisingly at home.\n---\n\n...\n\n**How it works**\n---\n\nWe begin with a short breathing and centring exercise, followed by simple rhythm demonstration and call and response drumming. We then move into smaller group discussion around a shared theme. From there we shift into collective jamming and improvisation, and end with a potluck meal and informal connection.\n---\n\n...\n**Typical meeting flow**\n\n1. 🫱🏽‍🫲🏻 Arrival & social time – 15 min\n2. 🙋🏻‍♀️ Welcome, check in and centring – 15 min\n3. 🪘 Call & Respond **Drumming & demo** – 20 min\n4. 💬 Facilitated **Discussion** on the Theme (groups of five-or so) – 20 min\n5. 🕺🏽 Open **Jamming** with multiple instruments – 30 min\n6. 🦋 Potluck **dinner** & social time afterwards – 60 min\n\n*This outline is flexible and may shift to suit the group and the space.*\n---\n\n...\n**Logistics & what to bring**\nWe meet in a large and beautiful space. Drums are available on a first come first served basis. We also provide plenty of small percussion instruments so every hand can play. You are welcome to bring your own drum or instrument.\n\nWe end the evening with a shared **potluck meal**, an extension of the circle where conversation and connection continue. Since the event is free, we warmly ask everyone to bring a small item to share if they are able. Simple finger foods and easy to serve savoury items are especially helpful, such as fruit, veggies and dip, wraps, sandwiches, hummus and pita, samosas, spring rolls, crackers and cheese, or other meal friendly bites. Sweet items are welcome too, but meal friendly contributions are especially appreciated.\n---\n\n...\n\n**Cost & contributions**\n---\n\nThis is a free event. If you are unable to bring food, you are welcome to make an optional contribution toward refreshments and materials by e-transfer to **hooshmandnyc@gmail.com**\n---\n\n...\n\n**Helpful notes**\n---\n\nNo prep needed. Doors open at 3:45 p.m. Please arrive by then so we can start at 4:00 p.m. sharp and keep the flow. Location and any last minute updates are posted on Meetup and in our WhatsApp group. We recommend joining the WhatsApp group (ask us for the link at the venue) for quick notices.\n---\n\n...\n**Life Between Gatherings**\nDrum & Soul does not begin and end with the monthly session. For those who want to continue beyond the gatherings and go deeper, we also have:\n\n• **Advanced sessions** for those who want to go further in drumming technique and explore the discussion themes more deeply in a smaller group\n\n• **Home or café meetups** for simple in-person connection, where a few participants can continue the conversation more personally and naturally\n\n• **Ongoing contact** so the spirit of the gathering can carry into everyday life through our own reflection, friendship and mutual encouragement\n\nOver time, these smaller spaces help strengthen connection, shared learning, and community life between sessions. Ask us about these features for more detail.\n---\n\n...\n**Why this matters**\nOur world is like a sick body, and is aching for a lasting remedy. We believe our special mission here is to nurture one another, define our roles in service to our fellow humans, and become living temples of unity. A meaningful growth unfolds through both self‑discovery and collective effort, and one cannot truly flourish without the other. Come open and prepared to learn, to offer your gifts, and to be strengthened by the power of community.\n\n*This ad is also posted in other groups*\n\n📷 Follow us on [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/artsoultoronto/)\n🎥 [A glimpse from one of our sessions](https://youtu.be/ejfeV1PF-0k)","startDate":"2026-10-04T20:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Toronto Baha'i Centre","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"288 Bloor St. West, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Art & Soul","url":"https://www.meetup.com/art-soul/"},"performer":"Art & Soul"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Badminton Enthusiast","url":"https://www.meetup.com/badminton-enthusiast/events/316325682/","description":"ATTENTION:\nDue to many first timers signed up the event but no show, I have no choice to charge the first timers $10 per person as deposit via etransfer to me no later then Friday night. There is no refund for no show. If you show up, then I will pay the balance back to you at the end of the badminton event. My email address is: [lingseilau@yahoo.com](mailto:lingseilau@yahoo.com)\n\nRacket & Birdies: Everyone has to bring your own racket and at least one birdie with you.\n\nCourt fee: It will be informed at the comment section by 4pm. Cost per person is either $216 (for 4 courts), $162 (for 3 courts) or $108 (for 2 courts) divided by the number of players attended. My email address for etransfer is: [lingseilau@yahoo.com](mailto:lingseilau@yahoo.com)","startDate":"2026-10-04T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Epic Badminto Club","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Scarborough","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"39 Bertrand Ave, Toronto, ON M1L 2P3, Scarborough, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Badminton Enthusiast","url":"https://www.meetup.com/badminton-enthusiast/"},"performer":"Badminton Enthusiast"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Dundas Peak and Tews Falls Hiking","url":"https://www.meetup.com/lookingforfriends-toronto/events/316782203/","description":"Join our WhatsApp group\n[https://chat.whatsapp.com/F7838OJWfkiAlMEyNffVfZ](https://chat.whatsapp.com/F7838OJWfkiAlMEyNffVfZ)\n\n* **Trail Information**\nHiking Dundas Peak and Tews Falls in the Spencer Gorge Conservation Area offers a scenic 1.8-mile trail featuring the 41-metre-high Tews Falls and panoramic gorge views, with visits now operating on a first-come, first-served basis as advance reservations are no longer required.\nLocation\\*\\*:\\*\\* 590 Harvest Road, Dundas, Ontario.\nLength\\*\\*:\\*\\* About 1.8 miles (2.9 km) round trip .\nDifficulty\\*\\*:\\*\\* Easy to moderate with some short stair sections and small hills.\nTime\\*\\*:\\*\\* Roughly 25 to 30 minutes of walking each way between the parking area, Tews Falls, and Dundas Peak.\n**Key Highlights**\nTews Falls: A stunning ribbon waterfall standing at 41 metres tall with dual viewing platforms.\nDundas Peak: A high rocky lookout point providing sweeping views over the city of Hamilton and the Dundas Valley.\n**Book Carpool or Driver**\n*\n[https://www.extremelyshy.com/toronto&f66v6t](https://www.extremelyshy.com/toronto&f66v6t)\n*\n* **Carpool**: You will be assigned to a vehicle. Let the driver scan your QR code to access your carpool service.\n* **Driver**: You will receive driver instruction in your confirmation email. Scan the QR code from the passenger to provide your carpool service to get paid\n\n**What’s included**\n\n* Gas, Vehicle use, Driver effort.\n* Split bill with your vehicle people if any other expense is exist.\n\n**Meeting and Pickup**\n\n* Meeting Time: 8:00 AM\n* Meeting Point: In front of Tim Hortons Dufferin Station 1094 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M6H 1M5\n* End Time: 6:00 PM\n* End Point: This activity ends back at the meeting point.\n\n**Refund Policy**\n\n* Refund Policy: Not refundable except if the event is canceled, rescheduled. Contact us by the end of the day.\n\n**Liability**\n\n* The organizer and any/all assistant organizers and other attendees are in no way responsible and liable for your personal safety and health state, before, during, and at any time after this event.\n* You acknowledge you are solely responsible for your health, safety, and well-being before, during, and at any time after the event as stated previously.\n* All attendees shall forever hold harmless the organizers and other attendees and unconditionally waive any liabilities resulting from attending and/or participating in this event.p","startDate":"2026-10-04T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Dufferin Subway Station","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1006 Dufferin Street, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Beach Volleyball Hiking - Looking for Friends? - Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/lookingforfriends-toronto/"},"performer":"Beach Volleyball Hiking - Looking for Friends? - Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Fall Walk: From Cabbagetown to Cherry Street 🌿 🍺","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316182317/","description":"# 🍂 Fall Walk: From Rosedale to Cherry Street 🌿\n\n### A Fall Walk Through Some of Toronto's Most Interesting Neighbourhoods\n\nLooking for a walk that gives you a little bit of everything?\nWe'll start in **Rosedale**, make our way through **Cabbagetown and Regent Park**, wander through the **Distillery District**, stop at **Biidaasige Park**, and finish with a well-earned meal at **Cherry Street Bar-B-Que**.\nAlong the way, we'll see some of the city's oldest neighbourhoods, newer communities, historic architecture, green spaces, and some pretty great views.\nIt's a longer walk, but the route is more about **exploring Toronto together** than trying to finish as quickly as possible.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll meet outside **Rosedale Station** and begin our walk through Rosedale Valley, following the tree-lined route toward Cabbagetown.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Walk through Rosedale Valley 🌳\n* Explore the historic streets of Cabbagetown\n* Pass through Regent Park\n* Wander through the Distillery District\n* Stop at Biidaasige Park\n* Take in the fall scenery and city views\n* Finish at **Cherry Street Bar-B-Que** 🍖\n\nThe walk includes a **long set of stairs**, so while this isn't a difficult hike, you should be comfortable walking for several hours and keeping up with the group.\n\n***\n\n## 🏙️ A Little Toronto History Along the Way\n\nThis walk takes us through several very different parts of Toronto.\nIn **Cabbagetown**, we'll pass beautifully preserved Victorian homes and streets that reflect the neighbourhood's long history, including its Irish roots.\n\nWe'll then make our way through **Regent Park**, one of Toronto's most historically significant communities, where older social housing has been joined by new housing, arts, and community spaces.\nFrom there, we'll head into the **Distillery District**, with its cobblestone streets and historic red-brick buildings.\n\nWe'll also stop at **Biidaasige Park**, whose name means *“the sun is shining”* in Anishinaabemowin.\nIt's a lot of Toronto in one walk.\n\n***\n\n## 🍺 The Keating Channel Pub & Grill\n\nWe'll finish our walk at **The Keating Channel Pub & Grill**, right on the Keating Channel.\n\nThere's a bit of history behind this stop. The pub struggled during the massive Port Lands construction, when road closures and the relocation of the Cherry Street bridge made the area difficult to reach. With the Port Lands now transformed and **Biidaasige Park** open, people are rediscovering this part of the city — and the pub is getting a second chance.\n\nAfter exploring the new park and the transformed Port Lands, we'll finish at one of the neighbourhood's old survivors: a casual waterfront pub with a patio overlooking the Keating Channel.\n\n***\n\n## ☀️ Weather & Expectations\n\nThis is a **long urban walk**, not a difficult hike, but you should be comfortable being on your feet for several hours.\nThere is a long set of stairs along the route.\nPlease wear comfortable walking shoes and dress appropriately for the weather.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Outside Rosedale Station\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** 11:00 AM sharp\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** Cherry Street Bar-B-Que\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧴 Sunscreen\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* People who enjoy exploring Toronto\n* Anyone who likes history and architecture\n* People looking for a longer social walk\n* Anyone who wants to discover neighbourhoods they might not normally visit\n* People who enjoy stopping for food at the end\n* Anyone who wants to spend a Sunday exploring the city with other people\n\nThe destination isn't really the point.\n**It's the people you meet along the way.**\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**.\n\n**Come for the walk.**\n**Stay for the friendship.**\n**And maybe stay a little longer for lunch.** 🍺🌿","startDate":"2026-10-04T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Rosedale Station","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":", Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🥂 Feel-Good Social for North York Locals & Newcomers — Good Vibes","url":"https://www.meetup.com/concrete-jungle-green-thumb-jam-sessions/events/316563142/","description":"🙌 Good to see you, North York crew.\n\nReally looking forward to meeting everyone really soon. 👋\n\n**[✨ TAP BELOW TO TAKE PART TODAY](https://meadowhollow12670.theliveround.com/product?productId=661.0&productType=onlineSpeedDating&city=North%20York&groupurlname=concrete-jungle-green-thumb-jam-sessions&face_v=100.0)**","startDate":"2026-10-04T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"49 Loire Valley Ave","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"49 Loire Valley Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Concrete Jungle Green Thumb Jam Sessions","url":"https://www.meetup.com/concrete-jungle-green-thumb-jam-sessions/"},"performer":"Concrete Jungle Green Thumb Jam Sessions"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"BRUNCH TIME!!!!! SUNDAY OCT 4 AT 12:30 PM ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/women-that/events/316729663/","description":"It seems like everyone loves Brunch. Extremely popular so please sign up as soon as possible. I picked Drunch Kitchen since it is a lovely setting with a very impressive menu","startDate":"2026-10-04T16:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMo